# Week 1 — Urdu OCR Project

Collecting and preparing Urdu text images for an Optical Character Recognition project.

## What This Week Was About

Week 1 focused on understanding the Urdu OCR problem, setting up the required tools, and collecting Urdu text images for the dataset.

## Why This Matters

OCR (Optical Character Recognition) converts text from images into machine-readable text. Urdu OCR is challenging because Urdu uses a connected script with different character shapes and writing patterns. An Urdu OCR system can be useful for digitizing Urdu books, newspapers, documents, and other printed material.

## What I Did

- Set up GitHub, Hugging Face, and Google Colab.
- Researched Optical Character Recognition.
- Studied why Urdu OCR is challenging.
- Collected Urdu text images.
- Organized the collected images into folders.
- Created a labels file containing the correct text for the images.

## Dataset

The Week 1 target was a minimum of 100 Urdu text images.

The images were collected from different sources such as:

- Urdu newspapers
- Urdu books
- Signboards
- Existing Urdu datasets
- Synthetic Urdu text images

## Results

- Urdu OCR dataset collection started.
- Images were organized into categories.
- Ground-truth labels were prepared.
- Dataset was made ready for the preprocessing stage.

